WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.912
Three groups of settings decide
whether the controller is auditable.

2
00:00:03.912 --> 00:00:05.276
First, sign-in.

3
00:00:05.276 --> 00:00:09.211
Federate it to your identity provider,
so your conditional access and

4
00:00:09.211 --> 00:00:13.350
phishing-resistant sign-in apply, and
keep local accounts for break-glass.

5
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.320
The default lifetime used
to be a thousand years,

6
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.587
and old tokens keep it, so
revoke them when you upgrade.

7
00:00:19.587 --> 00:00:21.012
Second, logging.

8
00:00:21.012 --> 00:00:25.700
Send everything to your SIEM, and set
the cleanup jobs to match your retention.

9
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.250
Third, content.

10
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.150
Hub signing is off by
default, so turn it on.

11
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.475
And project signing is the quiet hero,

12
00:00:32.475 --> 00:00:35.700
because a project that fails
its signature won't run.

13
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.037
That links the reviewed change
to what actually executes.

14
00:00:39.037 --> 00:00:41.420
Which brings us to the controller itself.
